From b7d213265d38442c72c3cd1f3844962ea032a844 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Assistant <assistant@example.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:51:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Move Office module pages to shared base.html layout

Converts 11 standalone Office-module templates to extend base.html
so they get the shared sidebar/menubar and single Logout, per the
project's global UI/navigation rules:

- accounts_admission_queue.html
- add_board_result.html
- add_ssc_registration.html
- add_subject.html
- certificate_list.html (was using its own hand-rolled duplicate sidebar)
- delete_ssc_registration.html
- delete_subject.html
- import_ssc_registrations.html
- issue_certificate.html (was using its own hand-rolled duplicate sidebar)
- issue_tc.html
- ssc_registration_list.html (was using its own hand-rolled duplicate sidebar)

All pages verified with Django test client (200 OK, sidebar + single
Logout present). public_admission_form.html and public_admission_success.html
intentionally left standalone since they are public-facing pages with
no login/sidebar context.
---
